%[text] # Autonomous Quadcopter: Guided Stage Walkthrough
%[text] Follow the demonstration from the requirements baseline to architecture, executable behavior, 3D flight, and the single approved verification test. Use **Run Section** to move at your own pace. You can also highlight one command and run that selection when you want to inspect a single artifact.
%[text] This is a plain-text MATLAB Live Script for R2025a or later. Its default actions open saved artifacts and display existing evidence. It does not run simulations or tests, save models or requirements, or regenerate checkpoint outputs.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Walkthrough sections"}
%%
%[text] ## Start here: workspace and stage map
%[text] Run this section first. Edit the project path if you move the demo. The stage switcher closes only clean demo models and refuses to discard unsaved model, requirements, link, or dictionary edits. Because all stages reuse model names, review one stage at a time.
projectRoot = 'C:\Demos\agentic-uav-mbse';
demoRoot = fullfile(projectRoot,'Quadcopter_Agentic_Demo');
assert(isfolder(demoRoot),'Update projectRoot to the location of this demo.');
addpath(projectRoot);
stageNames = ["01_Requirements_Architecture";"02_Executable_Model"; ...
    "03_3D_Flight_Simulation";"04_Path_Followed_Verification"];
stagePurpose = ["Baseline, architecture, interfaces, and allocation links"; ...
    "Closed-loop mission and low-fidelity vehicle behaviors"; ...
    "Opaque 3D quadcopter, waypoints, trajectory, and position plots"; ...
    "Approved FR-06-only Path Followed test and actual results"];
table(stageNames,stagePurpose,'VariableNames',{'Stage','ReviewFocus'}) %[output:7c23e0ed]
%%
%[text] ## Stage 01: requirements and top-level architecture
%[text] Open the unchanged Markdown baseline, the Requirements Editor, and the architecture. The baseline contains 18 identified requirements. FR-05 remains optional, and FR-06 is the sole formal verification target. This checkpoint contains architecture only, so do not try to simulate it.
stage1 = walkthrough_select_stage(projectRoot,'01_Requirements_Architecture'); %[output:5e493305]
architecture1 = systemcomposer.openModel(fullfile(stage1,'QuadArchitecture_AI.slx'));
requirements1 = slreq.open(fullfile(stage1,'Quadcopter_MVP_AI.slreqx'));
edit(fullfile(stage1,'Quadcopter_MVP_Requirements_v1.md'));
%%
%[text] ## Stage 02: executable system and mission inputs
%[text] Switch to the executable checkpoint. GroundControlStation sequences takeoff, three predefined waypoints, and landing using returned telemetry. VehicleModel contains the supported reduced-order Multirotor Guidance Model. Open the parameters to see the NED waypoint coordinates and control settings.
stage2 = walkthrough_select_stage(projectRoot,'02_Executable_Model'); %[output:56f4e66a]
architecture2 = systemcomposer.openModel(fullfile(stage2,'QuadArchitecture_AI.slx'));
requirements2 = slreq.open(fullfile(stage2,'Quadcopter_MVP_AI.slreqx'));
%%
%[text] ## Stage 02: saved smoke-run status and run entry point
%[text] Read the recorded smoke status and inspect the run helper. Opening the helper does not execute it. The landing behavior is an idealized near-ground proximity stop, not a physical ground-contact model. The stage README explains the execution settings and limitations.
smoke2 = jsondecode(fileread(fullfile(stage2,'smoke_status.json')));
table(smoke2.Compiles,smoke2.SimulationRuns,smoke2.EndTime,smoke2.SimulationWarnings, ...
    'VariableNames',{'ModelCompiled','SimulationRan','SimulatedSeconds','Warnings'})
edit(fullfile(stage2,'run_stage02_smoke.m'));
% edit(fullfile(stage2,'init_stage02.m'));
% edit(fullfile(stage2,'STAGE_README.md'));
%%
%[text] ## Stage 03: animation connections and coordinate convention
%[text] Open the Visualization behavior. Its native UAV Animation block receives NED position and scalar-first body-to-NED quaternion data, draws an opaque red multirotor, and displays the three waypoint markers and actual trajectory. R2026b converts the NED inputs to an ENU display. The adapter and review script document this convention and the camera framing.
stage3 = walkthrough_select_stage(projectRoot,'03_3D_Flight_Simulation'); %[output:6698048b]
architecture3 = systemcomposer.openModel(fullfile(stage3,'QuadArchitecture_AI.slx'));
requirements3 = slreq.open(fullfile(stage3,'Quadcopter_MVP_AI.slreqx'),'UAV-MVP-SV-02');
open_system(fullfile(stage3,'Visualization_MVP_AI.slx'));
%%
%[text] ## Stage 03: open the saved 3D flight and position plots
%[text] These interactive FIG files show the recorded final scene and the actual position/mode history. Rotate the 3D view to inspect the supported rotor-and-arm mesh. The figures are saved views, not a new simulation. The run helper can reproduce the moving mission from a working copy.
% openfig(fullfile(stage3,'flight_evidence','flight_3d_final.fig'),'new','visible');
% openfig(fullfile(stage3,'flight_evidence','mission_position_trajectory.fig'),'new','visible');
% flight3 = jsondecode(fileread(fullfile(stage3,'flight_status.json')));
% table(flight3.ModelCompiles,flight3.SimulationRuns,flight3.EndTime,flight3.SimulationWarnings, ...
%     'VariableNames',{'ModelCompiled','SimulationRan','SimulatedSeconds','Warnings'})
edit(fullfile(stage3,'run_stage03_flight.m'));
%%
%[text] ## Stage 04: the approved verification definition
%[text] This checkpoint formally verifies only **UAV-MVP-FR-06** through the single **Path Followed** case. The approved criterion is a 0.20 m 3D corridor around each active finite cruise-path segment, ordered waypoint arrival within 0.20 m, and path completion within 90 simulated seconds. Modes 2 through 4 are assessed; takeoff and landing performance are excluded.
stage4 = walkthrough_select_stage(projectRoot,'04_Path_Followed_Verification'); %[output:824707e8]
architecture4 = systemcomposer.openModel(fullfile(stage4,'QuadArchitecture_AI.slx'));
requirements4 = slreq.open(fullfile(stage4,'Quadcopter_MVP_AI.slreqx'),'UAV-MVP-FR-06');
testDefinition4 = sltest.testmanager.load(fullfile(stage4,'QuadcopterTests_AI.mldatx'));
sltest.testmanager.view;
% edit(fullfile(stage4,'PATH_FOLLOWED_CRITERIA.md'));
% edit(fullfile(stage4,'criteria_approval.json'));
% edit(fullfile(stage4,'stage04_path_metrics.m'));
edit(fullfile(stage4,'stage04_custom_criteria.m'));
%%
%[text] ## Stage 04: saved native results and requirement links
%[text] Import the saved result, then select Results and Artifacts in Test Manager. The result contains one passed case and three passed custom-criteria checks. In Requirements Editor, expand Links on FR-06 to follow FCS, Guidance, WaypointGuidance, and the Verified by Path Followed link. Refreshing the status reads the imported evidence; it does not execute a test.
sltest.testmanager.importResults(fullfile(stage4,'PathFollowed_Results.mldatx'));
sltest.testmanager.view;
updateVerificationStatus(requirements4);
slreq.open(requirements4,'UAV-MVP-FR-06');
verification4 = getVerificationStatus(find(requirements4,'Id','UAV-MVP-FR-06')) %[output:3f434de4]
%%
%[text] ## Stage 04: measured tracking evidence
%[text] Review the actual-versus-intended path, sampled errors, and ordered waypoint arrivals. The saved run measured a maximum error of approximately 0.1142 m against the approved 0.20 m limit. The following values are read from the saved metric file. RMS is descriptive, not an additional acceptance threshold.
metrics4 = jsondecode(fileread(fullfile(stage4,'PathFollowed_metrics.json')));
table(string(metrics4.Verdict),metrics4.ToleranceMeters,metrics4.OverallMaximumErrorMeters, ... %[output:group:337c1392] %[output:3b104e09]
    metrics4.OverallRMSErrorMeters,metrics4.EvaluatedPositionSamples, ... %[output:3b104e09]
    'VariableNames',{'Verdict','ApprovedLimitMeters','MaximumErrorMeters','RMSErrorMeters','AssessedSamples'}) %[output:group:337c1392] %[output:3b104e09]
struct2table(metrics4.LegStatistics) %[output:36c001a8]
openfig(fullfile(stage4,'verification_evidence','PathFollowed_tracking_evidence.fig'),'new','visible'); %[output:5a1f5f3c]
% edit(fullfile(stage4,'FR06_traceability.json'));
% edit(fullfile(stage4,'run_stage04_verification.m'));
% edit(fullfile(stage4,'STAGE_README.md'));
%%
%[text] ## Graphics: play the recorded flight GIF
%[text] Open the 2x-speed recorded-flight replay with the default Windows viewer. It shows the full mission with the red drone, waypoint labels, and a growing trajectory trail. The exporter source is also available for inspection; it reads recorded data without modifying stage checkpoints.
gifFile = fullfile(projectRoot,'graphics','quadcopter_path_following.gif');
winopen(gifFile);
edit(fullfile(projectRoot,'graphics','create_drone_path_gif.m'));
%%
%[text] ## Finish: what the saved result establishes
%[text] Only the agreed sampled cruise waypoint-following criterion for FR-06 is formally verified in the nominal simulated conditions. Other functional, architecture, and visualization requirements have design or demonstration evidence, not separate formal passing verdicts. This result does not establish flight safety, hardware readiness, physical touchdown, or overall UAV compliance.
%[text] To regenerate simulation or test outputs, first copy the relevant stage into a new working folder and use its run helper there. The stage run helpers write output files; this walkthrough deliberately opens them for inspection instead of invoking them. Keep the four checkpoints unchanged.
%[text] The only support function used by this walkthrough is `walkthrough_select_stage.m` beside this file. It performs stage switching and places any incidental generated cache outside the checkpoints in `walkthrough_workspace`.

